data.body:
Samples often differ in one or two keys (a particle, an energy, a seed) and agree on the rest. Until now each sample had to repeat its whole generation and simulation, and a forgotten `physics.list` would quietly change one sample's physics. This PR adds a top-level `stages` block, so the shared part is written once.

**Behavior.** `stages` maps a stage type to what that stage of every sample starts from:

```yaml
stages:
  generation: {executor: gun, particle: gamma, direction: {distribution: uniform, theta: [80, 100], phi: [0, 360], unit: deg}}
  simulation: {executor: ddsim, events: 1000, physics.list: FTFP_BERT}
samples:
  gamma_10gev: {generation: {energy: {value: 10, unit: GeV}}, simulation: {seed: 42}}
  gamma_50gev: {generation: {energy: {value: 50, unit: GeV}}, simulation: {seed: …
